{"id": "20568349", "revid": "2842084", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20568349", "title": "William Lofgren", "text": "William Lofgren (February 14, 1913 \u2013 June 11, 2004) was an American canoeist who competed in the 1936 Summer Olympics.\nHe was born in Brooklyn, New York and died in Phoenix, Arizona. Lofgren served in the United States Army during World War II in both China and India as a technical sergeant.\nIn 1936, Lofgren and his partner William Gaehler finished seventh in the K-2 10000 metres competition."}
