{"id": "20569851", "revid": "48282118", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20569851", "title": "Landfermann-Gymnasium", "text": "Landfermann-Gymnasium (LfG) is situated in the city centre of Duisburg, Germany. It is a municipal grammar school for boys and girls, and is one of the oldest schools in Germany.\nFounded before 1280, it was named as Schola Duisburgensis, the school was transformed into a Latin school in 1559, which today's Landfermann-Gymnasium acknowledges as its official founding year. In 1925, it was renamed after Dietrich Wilhelm Landfermann (1800\u20131882), who was head of the school from 1835-1841."}
