{"id": "20570204", "revid": "43682176", "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=20570204", "title": "Elizabeth Ryan (swimmer)", "text": "Elizabeth M. Ryan (January 4, 1923 \u2013 May 1998) was an American competition swimmer who represented the United States at the 1936 Summer Olympics in Berlin, Germany. As a 13-year-old, Ryan swam for the third-place U.S. team in the preliminary heats of the women's 4\u00d7100-meter freestyle relay, helping the Americans qualify for the event final. Under the 1936 Olympic swimming rules, she did not receive a medal because she did not swim in the final."}
